# Aci Sh.A

I am trying to make an e-commerce app for a company located in Albania, called Aci Sh.A. It sells it's oil products ( for cars ) online, and we need to make the code as easy to manage in the future, as idempotent and as refactorable as possible.

- Never use the default import of React. 
Always use named exports for variables, types, components.
It's more clear that way.
- Always look for idempotent solutions.
- Never use classes.
- Always use types and not interfaces.
- Optimize re-renders.
- Handle a good shopping cart / context logic.

How this project is set up ?
1. I use NextJs, Typescript, Biome, Tailwind, ShadCn.
2. I use the Supabase API to integrate a messaging feature, where users can leave a message and it gets stored there until an admin sees the message.
3. The backend is provided by my friend and is written in Python with Django REST.
4. Below is an list of API's that the backend exposes.

    a. If path is localhost:8000/product  :
      Using the URLconf defined in ACIBackEnd.urls, Django tried these URL patterns, in this order:
        product/ list/ [name='product-list']
        product/ list<drf_format_suffix:format> [name='product-list']
        product/ create/ [name='product-create']
        product/ create<drf_format_suffix:format> [name='product-create']
        product/ update/<int:pk>/ [name='product-update']
        product/ update/<int:pk><drf_format_suffix:format> [name='product-update']
        product/ category/list/create/ [name='category-list-create']
        product/ category/list/create<drf_format_suffix:format> [name='category-list-create']
        product/ brand/list/create/ [name='brand-list-create']
        product/ brand/list/create<drf_format_suffix:format> [name='brand-list-create']
        product/ order/create/ [name='order-create']
        product/ order/create<drf_format_suffix:format> [name='order-create']
        product/ order/list/ [name='order-list']
        product/ order/list<drf_format_suffix:format> [name='order-list']
        product/ discount/set/
        product/ discount/set<drf_format_suffix:format>
    The API structure is kinda messy for me so I am relying on you to provide the correct paths and correct params for the API request to be successful.
With that said, that's all the rules for now. You can go and solve the stupid problems that I can not :)).